      "body": "Audit acceptance now binds the admitted native auditor, original streams, reports, source subjects and retained artifacts. Missing, changed or incomplete observations refuse; failure artifacts preserve the primary outcome. Audit capture uses the Rust helper through canonical dispatchers.\n\nHosted tests previously inherited GitHub Runner.Worker IPC pipes and correctly failed descriptor admission. The CI launcher now marks only the observed, identity-matched channel pair close-on-exec; unrelated descriptors and the native hostile-descriptor tests remain unchanged. Bounded failure diagnostics retain metadata without descriptor contents or credentials.\n\nValidation on f6033ea: canonical local required lane passed 62 fast and 271 contract tests, lint, security, docs and corpus replay. Push and PR required workflows both passed. Four actual fork/exec tests cover eight transport scenarios. Historical failed runs are retained.\n\nThis is component/CI acceptance. It does not qualify a signed auditor distribution, installed coding service, provider execution or complete product release. Independent review remains required before integration.\n",
