      "body": "## The defect\n\nEvery completed attempt preserved its Candidate and then failed. The Runner releases its lease as `Succeeded` before asking gitd to delete the workspace \u2014 an order pinned by a simulation test, so that a crash between the two leaves a recorded Candidate rather than an unaccounted workspace. Cleanup then took a Kernel mutation permit like any other write, and minting one performs an online lease and fence read-back that the release has just made impossible.\n\nReproduced three ways: on the simulator, on the retained real Claude recording, and this morning through the real dispatch path (farmd + production gitd + the product Runner), whose journal reads `candidate_prepared` \u2192 `candidate_preserved` \u2192 `released: succeeded` \u2192 `terminated: GITD_REFUSED` with `AUTHORITY_REFUSED: online lease/fence read-back refused \u2026 no active lease`.\n\nThe Runner's own source named this a known contradiction and said the resolution belonged here, because cleanup is documented as receipt-gated.\n\n## The change\n\n`handle_cleanup` verifies the session token, refuses a frozen daemon, then calls the new `PreservationAuthority::authorize_receipt` **before any reservation** \u2014 seal, state digest, cleanup target, destination identity, artifact shape, salvaged objects, bundle and artifact digest. It reserves through the new `authorize_by_preservation_receipt`, which computes the same transport fingerprint as the Kernel path and builds a complete `MutationSubject` from the receipt digest, the operation and the session's exact writer incarnation, but consults no online checker. Settlement is recorded in the durable mutation ledger with no Kernel round trip; an indeterminate outcome still freezes the daemon.\n\nEvery other operation keeps the Kernel permit path unchanged, and those signatures are untouched.\n\n## Proof\n\n- `cargo test --locked -p bullet-gitd -p bullet-git-workspace` \u2014 171 passed, 0 failed\n- `cargo test --locked --all-features -p bullet-gitd` \u2014 72 passed, 0 failed\n- `cargo clippy --locked \u2026 --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo fmt --check` \u2014 clean\n\nEleven new tests: cleanup succeeds against a checker that can issue no permit while another operation on the same daemon still refuses `AUTHORITY_CONTRACT_UNAVAILABLE`; garbage, empty, byte-tampered and foreign-session receipts each refuse `PRESERVATION_RECEIPT_REFUSED`, leave the session usable, and the real receipt then still cleans up; reservation replay returns the durable result and never a second permit; a mismatching replay refuses `AUTHORITY_REPLAY_CONFLICT`; a post-permit repository failure still yields `MUTATION_OUTCOME_UNKNOWN` and freezes.\n\n## Not in this PR\n\nThe matching Runner change (stop minting a permit for cleanup; report a post-preservation cleanup failure as `WORKSPACE_ORPHANED_AFTER_PRESERVATION` naming the candidate, receipt and destination) is prepared as a reviewed patch and handed to the kernel's integrator, whose tree is frozen for a qualification window. `apply_change` still consumes its permit before repository validation; closing that needs a read-only validator in files outside this change's scope.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_015qHQABNS382h2gi5jb5oUY",
